  title: "What a larger ELBO does—and does not—show",
  color: red.darken(10%),
)[
  For a fixed model and family, a larger ELBO means a smaller reverse-KL gap. It does not by itself show calibrated uncertainty, useful latent variables, a correct generative model, or larger evidence than a different model whose variational gap is different.
]

